isSyzygy -- Tests if a module is a d-th syzygy
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isSyzygy(M,d)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, over a polynomial ring.
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, positive
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, returns true if M is
        a d-th syzygy, and false otherwise.

Description
===========

This algorithm is based upon the methods described in the book of Evans and
Griffith (Syzygies. London Mathematical Society Lecture Note Series, 106.
Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, 1985.)

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : kk=ZZ/32003                      |
|                                      |
|o1 = kk                               |
|                                      |
|o1 : QuotientRing                     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : S=kk[a..d]                       |
|                                      |
|o2 = S                                |
|                                      |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                   |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : F=res (ideal vars S)^2           |
|                                      |
|      1      10      20      15      4|
|o3 = S  <-- S   <-- S   <-- S   <-- S |
|                                      |
|     0      1       2       3       4 |
|                                      |
|o3 : Complex                          |
+--------------------------------------+

NOTE:  We are viewing a syzygy module as a cokernel of an appropriate map.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isSyzygy(coker F.dd_3,3)  -- the cokernel defined by the 3rd map is not |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = false                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|a 3rd syzygy                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isSyzygy(coker F.dd_4,3)  -- the cokernel defined by the 4th map is a   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = true                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3rd syzygy                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

